1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,776
Sharp pain in your upper right belly after a fatty meal, plus eyes turning a little yellow?

2
00:00:05,144 --> 00:00:07,918
That points to your gallbladder, not just your stomach.

3
00:00:08,286 --> 00:00:14,199
In the US, gallstones cause 35 to 40 percent of acute pancreatitis cases - the top cause.

4
00:00:14,567 --> 00:00:18,937
Your gallbladder and pancreas share one drainage opening into the small intestine.

5
00:00:19,305 --> 00:00:24,920
When a stone blocks it, digestive enzymes back up into the pancreas and it starts digesting itself.

6
00:00:25,288 --> 00:00:27,074
Crash dieting raises that risk.

7
00:00:27,442 --> 00:00:35,114
Losing weight too fast makes your liver dump extra cholesterol into bile faster than your gallbladder can handle, so it crystallizes into stones.

8
00:00:35,482 --> 00:00:39,622
A diet low in fiber, fruit, and vegetables is linked to more gallstones too.

9
00:00:39,990 --> 00:00:44,957
If you are losing weight, aim for about half a kilogram to one kilogram a week, not a crash.

10
00:00:45,325 --> 00:00:51,536
Add beans, oats, and vegetables for fiber, and keep some healthy fat in meals - it helps your gallbladder empty regularly.

11
00:00:51,904 --> 00:00:58,372
Pain that will not quit, fever, or yellowing skin and eyes means an ER visit, not wait and see.
